MOD_DSP=auto: pitch envelope and COLOR MOD on DSP B
s1m0    528 instructions, 2112 halfwords
s1m1    627 instructions, 2777 halfwords
s1mm1     7 instructions, 44 halfwords
s1c0      2 instructions, 7 halfwords
s1c1      2 instructions, 7 halfwords
kernel per voice: A 127 lines, 10 words; B 56 lines, 19 words
A -> B x: race (voices 0); same sample (voices 1,2,3,4)
A -> B input pitch: same sample (voices 0,1,2,3,4)
A -> B gate / trigger copies: same sample (voices 0,1,2,3,4)
note: DSP A has 4 spill words and does not use r5 / r6: SYSTEM-S1CC has no host keeping them, build the kernel with --regs 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 (docs/S1CC.md §1.1)
note: DSP B has 1 spill words and does not use r5 / r6: SYSTEM-S1CC has no host keeping them, build the kernel with --regs 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 (docs/S1CC.md §1.1)
